{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DirectoryConfig\/groupMappings"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DirectoryConfig"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"groupMappings","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12GroupMappingV","text":"GroupMapping","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/GroupMapping"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/directoryconfig\/groupmappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The group-mapping table (D-30): which directory groups put a user into which AXIAM"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"groups. Empty means no directory group maps to anything, and a sign-in then removes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every directory-sourced membership the user held."}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","title":"groupMappings","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK15DirectoryConfigV13groupMappingsSayAA12GroupMappingVGvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"groupMappings","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"GroupMapping","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12GroupMappingV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}]},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DirectoryConfig":{"type":"topic","title":"DirectoryConfig","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tenant’s directory configuration, as stored and as read back. Carries no secret: see the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module documentation."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/directoryconfig","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DirectoryConfig","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectoryConfig"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectoryConfig"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DirectoryConfig/groupMappings":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The group-mapping table (D-30): which directory groups put a user into which AXIAM"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"groups. Empty means no directory group maps to anything, and a sign-in then removes","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every directory-sourced membership the user held."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"groupMappings"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12GroupMappingV","text":"GroupMapping","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"groupMappings","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DirectoryConfig\/groupMappings","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/directoryconfig\/groupmappings"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/GroupMapping":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GroupMapping"}],"title":"GroupMapping","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/GroupMapping","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One row of the group-mapping table (G-3, T23.3.4, D-30): a directory group, named by its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distinguished name, and the AXIAM group a member of it is put into. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table is the only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"way a directory group reaches an AXIAM group."}]},{"type":"text","text":" There is no match by name, no prefix or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wildcard, and no AXIAM group is ever created from a directory one: a directory administrator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"who names a group "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"admins"},{"type":"text","text":" gains nothing unless a tenant administrator mapped it here. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"DN is stored as the administrator typed it and compared after RFC 4514 normalisation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam_directory::dn"},{"type":"text","text":"), so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CN=Staff, OU=Groups"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cn=staff,ou=groups"},{"type":"text","text":" are the same row."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"One DN may map to several AXIAM groups; the same (DN, group) pair twice is refused as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"redundant."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GroupMapping"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/groupmapping","role":"symbol"}}}